@tradition whodunnit-club
// Round 2: Lars Achterberg reads a short mystery aloud in three parts; after each, everyone writes down who did it. Every 4 weeks from week 6 (Days 38, 66...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1306
title: Whodunnit club
when: every 4 weeks wednesday week 2 from day 36
at: 19:30-20:30
min: 20
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: achterberg-lars always, moreau-signe always, quist-ilse always, quiet-corner 40%, everyone 10%
anim: read
host: achterberg-lars
from: achterberg-lars
invite: host=achterberg-lars odds=25% line="Whodunnit club. Three parts, one culprit. Write your guess. Don't guess early."

== mail
- Whodunnit club tomorrow, {time}, the bow lounge. I read a short mystery in three parts; after each, you write who did it. Somebody always guesses too early.

== ask
- Whodunnit club in the bow lounge. Lars reads. Everyone accuses everyone.   #funny
- Mystery night. I already know who did it. I always already know.   #funny
- Coming to whodunnit club? Bring a pencil and a suspicious mind.

== here
- It's the gardener. It's always the gardener.   #funny
- Write it down. No changing it later.
- Wait. Read that bit again.
- I knew it! No. I didn't know it.   #funny

== thanks
- Lars reads a short mystery aloud in three parts, and after each one everybody writes down who did it. Somebody guesses too early, and is right.   #funny

== chatter
- Somebody guessed the culprit in the first five minutes at whodunnit club. Again.   #funny
- Lars reads the clues in a very flat voice. It makes them worse. Better. Worse.   #funny
- Whodunnit club. I was wrong three times in one evening. A record.   #funny
